@ BIOS SWI 0x6 = Div
bios_div:
    svc 0x6                                  @ 0810e3fc 06df
    bx lr                                    @ 0810e3fe 7047

@ Invokes BIOS SVC 0x6 (Div, r0/r1 inputs); BIOS writes quotient to r0 and remainder to r1. Then `adds r0,r1,#0` overwrites r0 with r1 (remainder) and returns the remainder. Sibling of bios_div (0x0810e3fc, returns quotient directly); bios_div preserves the quotient, this function discards it and returns the remainder. Heavily called (~33 callers) by scene_pack / card_image regions for modulo operations such as sprite row/column coordinate computation.
@ 
@ Constants:
@ BIOS_DIV=SVC 0x6 (Div: r0=numerator, r1=denominator -> r0=quotient, r1=remainder)
get_bios_div_remainder:
    svc 0x6                                  @ 0810e400 06df
    adds r0,r1,#0x0    @ 0810e402 081c
    bx lr                                    @ 0810e404 7047
    .byte  0x00, 0x00

@ Invokes BIOS SVC 0xd (BiosCheckSum), subtracts the official GBA BIOS checksum constant 0xbaae187f from the return value, then ANDs with 0x1 to extract bit0 parity. Returns 0 if BIOS is intact and unmodified; returns 1 otherwise. Used for runtime BIOS integrity verification. Called by FUN_080f4c14 (dma;sys;display region) during DMA / display system initialization.
@ 
@ Constants:
@ BIOS_CHECKSUM_SVC=SVC 0xd (BiosCheckSum)
@ OFFICIAL_CRC=0xbaae187f (official GBA BIOS checksum constant)
@ PARITY_MASK=0x1 (bit0 parity mask)
check_bios_checksum_parity:
    svc 0xd                                  @ 0810e408 0ddf
    ldr r1, DAT_0810e414                     @ 0810e40a 0249
    subs r0,r0,r1    @ 0810e40c 401a
    movs r1,#0x1    @ 0810e40e 0121
    ands r0,r1    @ 0810e410 0840
    bx lr                                    @ 0810e412 7047
DAT_0810e414:
    .word  0xbaae187f                     @ 0810e414 7f18aeba

